WEBVTT

00:07.841 --> 00:11.011
Swear to me that everything you said
about the Fireflies is true.

00:16.057 --> 00:17.350
I swear.

00:32.615 --> 00:33.616
Okay.

01:46.231 --> 01:48.066
Why would he do this?

01:48.775 --> 01:50.068
I heard rumors.

01:51.027 --> 01:53.362
It was some kid he took
that was supposedly--

01:53.363 --> 01:56.240
- That wasn't true.
- Supposedly what?

01:56.241 --> 01:58.368
Something not true.

01:59.244 --> 02:00.828
Because it isn't possible.

02:00.829 --> 02:03.123
No. Probably not.

02:03.832 --> 02:05.916
And even if it were,
it doesn't fucking matter anyway.

02:05.917 --> 02:07.418
- Not without--
- Enough.

02:11.089 --> 02:12.924
You want to worry about something,
worry about us.

02:15.552 --> 02:19.179
So, what do we do?
Do we look for other Fireflies?

02:19.180 --> 02:20.723
Where?

02:22.600 --> 02:24.644
This place was the Fireflies.

02:27.063 --> 02:29.898
Ed has a brother
who runs an outfit in Seattle.

02:29.899 --> 02:33.318
A guy named Isaac.
Supposedly, he'd take us all in.

02:33.319 --> 02:35.196
Not until we find Joel.

02:39.868 --> 02:43.036
We're finding him. Yes, we are.

02:43.037 --> 02:44.581
Yes, we are.

02:47.333 --> 02:48.668
Alright, let's talk about how.

02:49.878 --> 02:51.128
Because here's what we got.

02:51.129 --> 02:53.589
He's a smuggler.
His name's Joel or Joe.

02:53.590 --> 02:55.007
There's some confusion about that--

02:55.008 --> 02:58.635
Fifties, graying, beard, six foot tall,
scar on his right temple.

02:58.636 --> 03:00.429
Oh, yeah.
They say he's handsome.

03:00.430 --> 03:01.513
I forgot.

03:01.514 --> 03:04.099
With a three-day jump on us.
We should have gone right after him.

03:04.100 --> 03:06.143
He drove away, Abby.
In our only working vehicle.

03:06.144 --> 03:07.645
And we were trying to save the wounded.

03:09.522 --> 03:12.400
But we didn't save anyone, did we?

03:15.195 --> 03:17.279
- It's not fucking fair.
- No.

03:17.280 --> 03:19.907
None of this is fucking fair.

03:19.908 --> 03:21.409
Abby.

03:25.455 --> 03:26.497
Maybe,

03:27.999 --> 03:30.293
maybe the Seattle crew has resources.

03:33.004 --> 03:34.756
They could help us get some sort of lead.

03:39.177 --> 03:40.636
You'll help me find him.

03:40.637 --> 03:44.015
Yes. We'll help you find him.

03:47.143 --> 03:48.853
Then, we'll help you kill him.

04:37.944 --> 04:39.028
Slowly.

04:40.071 --> 04:41.072
What?

04:44.909 --> 04:46.369
When we kill him,

04:50.123 --> 04:51.749
we kill him slowly.

06:13.456 --> 06:14.791
Get up.

07:03.089 --> 07:05.882
Okay. Okay.

07:05.883 --> 07:07.176
Ellie!

07:13.599 --> 07:15.101
Boom, motherfucker.

07:15.726 --> 07:18.019
First of all, "okay" means stop.

07:18.020 --> 07:19.813
Sorry, I was in the moment.

07:19.814 --> 07:21.731
Second, you can't
"Boom, motherfucker" people

07:21.732 --> 07:23.191
who land the first hit on you.

07:23.192 --> 07:24.651
Square in the face, by the way.

07:24.652 --> 07:27.404
Well, I can obviously take a punch,
so who cares?

07:27.405 --> 07:29.614
- Fuckin' hard, by the way.
- I pulled it.

07:29.615 --> 07:31.867
- You pulled it?
- Yeah, he pulled it.

07:31.868 --> 07:33.577
- Why?
- 'Cause I told him to.

07:33.578 --> 07:36.163
- Why?
- Otherwise, he would have knocked you out.

07:36.164 --> 07:38.583
And I don't want to have
to explain that to Joel.

07:41.752 --> 07:42.920
Don't do that again.

07:43.504 --> 07:44.505
Okay.

07:47.925 --> 07:50.887
I should've closed in faster on that one,
but the rest was good.

07:52.054 --> 07:53.347
The rest was good.

07:56.142 --> 07:58.518
Are you going to the thing tonight?

07:58.519 --> 08:02.063
Don't we have to?
'Cause community and shit?

08:02.064 --> 08:04.108
You're part of the community now?

08:07.403 --> 08:10.155
Seriously, though, if you are,
we could use an extra pair of hands

08:10.156 --> 08:11.824
breaking down firewood for the cookout.

08:14.827 --> 08:16.120
Don't pull punches.

09:00.873 --> 09:01.873
Oh.

09:01.874 --> 09:03.292
Well, that's fucked.

09:28.109 --> 09:29.277
Hey.

09:30.069 --> 09:31.279
Hey, kiddo.

09:33.322 --> 09:34.656
Somethin' go wrong out there?

09:34.657 --> 09:38.868
Well, the main lines are clay,
all cracked to shit and full of roots.

09:38.869 --> 09:42.748
We're not sure what we're supposed to do,
and our foreman isn't foreman-ing.

09:45.084 --> 09:47.003
Yeah, sorry.
I'll be out there in a minute.

09:49.046 --> 09:51.673
- Whatcha doin'?
- Fixing these breakers.

09:51.674 --> 09:54.468
They were gonna chuck the whole panel
but all they need is new springs.

09:59.056 --> 10:00.057
Teach me?

10:03.811 --> 10:04.812
Okay.

10:06.731 --> 10:08.024
Well...

10:09.609 --> 10:12.277
First thing first,
before you mess with circuits,

10:12.278 --> 10:13.695
you gotta check if the wires are live.

10:13.696 --> 10:15.280
So, how do you do that?

10:15.281 --> 10:16.532
I...

10:17.325 --> 10:18.492
lick them?

10:21.621 --> 10:23.372
Voltage tester.

10:25.583 --> 10:29.461
Now, this right here
is the part that matters.

10:29.462 --> 10:31.087
Bimetallic strip.

10:31.088 --> 10:33.965
Too much current runs through,
heats up the strip,

10:33.966 --> 10:35.843
it bends, releases the lever?

10:36.302 --> 10:37.552
Circuit breaks.

10:37.553 --> 10:39.054
Otherwise,
the wires get hotter and hotter,

10:39.055 --> 10:41.222
lights the inside of your walls on fire.

10:41.223 --> 10:42.558
There goes your house.

10:43.351 --> 10:45.311
- Can I ask a question?
- Shoot.

10:46.520 --> 10:48.773
Why is she angry at you?

10:52.443 --> 10:55.863
- She said she was angry?
- No, but...

11:01.160 --> 11:03.037
You're her best friend,
reckon she would have told you.

11:04.455 --> 11:05.498
Nope.

11:11.921 --> 11:14.130
Well, I figure it's normal.

11:14.131 --> 11:18.468
Her bein' 19 and me bein' her, what I am.

11:18.469 --> 11:21.930
No one likes their parents at that age.
I never got there with my own kid,

11:21.931 --> 11:24.642
so we're both just figuring it out
for the first time, is all.

11:26.519 --> 11:27.645
We'll get through it.

11:28.813 --> 11:30.690
Yeah, that makes sense.

11:31.774 --> 11:34.276
- So, the springs hold the levers back--
- The thing is, I try.

11:36.404 --> 11:38.530
I know I'm a hard-ass
and maybe overprotective,

11:38.531 --> 11:39.865
and she's

11:41.200 --> 11:43.369
her, but...

11:45.830 --> 11:47.998
I mean, what did I do?

11:49.834 --> 11:51.043
I don't know.

11:53.921 --> 11:55.214
Yeah, well.

11:57.800 --> 12:01.303
I can't hold myself responsible
for another person's emotional state.

12:04.306 --> 12:06.475
Are you in fucking therapy?

12:07.560 --> 12:09.144
Holy shit, you're seeing Gail?

12:09.145 --> 12:11.147
I'm not in therapy. Jesus, go,

12:12.314 --> 12:14.190
go fix the main line.

12:14.191 --> 12:15.859
Saw out the cracked parts,

12:15.860 --> 12:18.111
pull the roots and we'll fill in the gaps
with some ABS.

12:18.112 --> 12:19.488
Go on.

12:24.118 --> 12:25.578
It'll be okay.

12:31.917 --> 12:32.918
Dina.

12:37.757 --> 12:39.759
Don't tell anyone I'm in therapy.

13:03.282 --> 13:05.074
Oh, shit.

13:05.075 --> 13:06.951
This scope is sick.

13:06.952 --> 13:09.788
It ain't the scope, it's the shooter.

13:09.789 --> 13:12.332
- You're gettin' good.
- Who's next?

13:12.333 --> 13:13.667
Let's see.

13:14.668 --> 13:17.838
Ah, okay.
There's a cluster of 'em up by the road.

13:18.547 --> 13:20.758
- One's broken away, you see him?
- See him.

13:21.717 --> 13:23.594
Alright, you wanna take your time
with this one.

13:24.345 --> 13:25.763
It's further away, so more drop.

13:26.764 --> 13:28.641
He's going uphill,
so you gotta compensate.

13:30.351 --> 13:31.935
Head shot?

13:31.936 --> 13:33.437
Always.

13:42.738 --> 13:45.032
- Ah, fuck.
- Nah.

13:46.033 --> 13:47.951
It's alright, you got him anyway.

13:47.952 --> 13:50.120
I guess. A lot of them out there.

13:51.080 --> 13:54.041
Yeah, I noticed.
Probably followin' down Route 89.

13:55.918 --> 13:58.337
Maybe comin' outta Alpine.

13:59.380 --> 14:02.048
We should head back.
I wanna get a patrol out there.

14:02.049 --> 14:04.218
Cool, I'll do that run.

14:05.302 --> 14:09.055
Actually,
I'm takin' you off patrols for a bit.

14:09.056 --> 14:10.348
Puttin' you on gate watch.

14:10.349 --> 14:12.226
Gate watch? What? Why?

14:13.936 --> 14:15.186
'Cause it's an important job.

14:15.187 --> 14:17.565
It's standing on a fucking fence.

14:18.357 --> 14:19.859
He's concerned about you.

14:20.860 --> 14:22.861
Unfucking real.

14:22.862 --> 14:25.572
Well, you know, last run,
you were a bit reckless.

14:25.573 --> 14:27.907
It was two runners and a Clicker
who barely had teeth.

14:27.908 --> 14:29.784
I handled it. Isn't that the job?

14:29.785 --> 14:31.661
You wandered off on your own, Ellie.

14:31.662 --> 14:33.788
- We have rules for reasons.
- Oh, please, Dina does this shit

14:33.789 --> 14:35.915
all the time, no one's putting her
on the fucking fence.

14:35.916 --> 14:39.794
Tommy, I'm an adult.
He can't tell me what I can and can't do.

14:39.795 --> 14:41.589
Yeah, well, he can tell me.

14:43.215 --> 14:45.758
Look, I've been dealin' with him
my whole life.

14:45.759 --> 14:48.261
Sometimes, easier to just go along.

14:48.262 --> 14:50.555
I don't care if it's easier.
It's not fair.

14:50.556 --> 14:52.015
And by the way, you know I'm the one

14:52.016 --> 14:53.975
we should be least worried about
when it comes to infected.

14:53.976 --> 14:57.020
Hey, no. You swore.
We don't talk about that.

14:57.021 --> 14:58.897
I got bit on my arm.

14:58.898 --> 15:01.650
Ellie, we don't talk about that.

15:03.193 --> 15:04.986
- I got bit, everybody!
- Hey!

15:04.987 --> 15:07.196
- I got bit!
- Hey! Hey, hey!

15:07.197 --> 15:09.741
I'm immune!

15:09.742 --> 15:11.535
Hey! Jesus.

15:12.119 --> 15:13.412
Goddammit.

15:14.538 --> 15:18.166
I swear, you and my brother?
Same goddamn fuckin' person.

15:18.167 --> 15:21.253
Well, if we're the same person,
you know you're not winning this.

15:24.423 --> 15:25.841
Put me on the patrol.

15:30.554 --> 15:32.139
Alpine run leaves at 1300.

15:37.353 --> 15:39.812
Now, you follow the rules.

15:39.813 --> 15:41.148
You obey your captain.

15:41.774 --> 15:43.399
No questions, no exceptions.

15:43.400 --> 15:45.736
Well, that depends. Who's the captain?

15:46.403 --> 15:49.572
- Ellie.
- Okay, fine. Whatever.

15:49.573 --> 15:51.158
I'll do it by the book.

15:58.248 --> 16:00.167
Easy girl. Come on.

16:05.255 --> 16:06.548
Open it up!

16:19.019 --> 16:21.479
These three will be done
by next day or so.

16:21.480 --> 16:23.398
Then another day to hook up sewage.

16:23.399 --> 16:26.901
Now, y'all wanted the library
and the school restored by spring.

16:26.902 --> 16:28.528
But they both need new roofs.

16:28.529 --> 16:31.114
With the manpower that we have,
I don't see any of this

16:31.115 --> 16:32.658
gettin' done until summer.

16:33.826 --> 16:36.370
This window isn't keepin'
the cold out anymore.

16:36.996 --> 16:40.124
Yeah, yeah. Caulk.
It's high up on my list.

16:41.000 --> 16:42.959
We've been using a ton of it
to restore the new--

16:42.960 --> 16:45.421
- We need to build faster.
- Faster?

16:46.880 --> 16:48.339
Sure. How much faster?

16:48.340 --> 16:52.719
See, we got this dial
called the Constructo meter.

16:52.720 --> 16:54.637
- Joel.
- The more you turn it, the faster we go.

16:54.638 --> 16:56.431
We're running out of space
to put these people.

16:56.432 --> 16:57.515
Yeah, I noticed.

16:57.516 --> 17:00.935
Maybe your council
would stop lettin' so many of 'em in.

17:00.936 --> 17:02.562
It's our council.

17:02.563 --> 17:04.522
And those people are fleeing
collapsed settlements.

17:04.523 --> 17:06.649
They're fleeing infected.
We're supposed to leave them out there?

17:06.650 --> 17:09.945
If our lifeboat is swamped,
yeah, we leave 'em out there.

17:17.745 --> 17:20.621
If I could, I'd let 'em all in.

17:20.622 --> 17:24.917
And I'm workin' every damn day and night
to make more space, you know that.

17:24.918 --> 17:28.005
But you got to look after your own first,
or you're no good to anyone.

17:30.382 --> 17:32.050
- Uncle Joel.
- Hey, buddy.

17:32.051 --> 17:34.887
- What are those?
- Come here.

17:36.889 --> 17:38.181
Okay, we're lookin' at maps.

17:38.182 --> 17:40.768
See? This is where we live.

17:41.810 --> 17:43.770
- And what's that?
- The fence.

17:43.771 --> 17:45.438
- And what's inside?
- People!

17:45.439 --> 17:47.565
- And what's outside?
- Monsters.

17:47.566 --> 17:49.233
That's right. And how do we keep 'em out?

17:49.234 --> 17:52.195
- We shoot them.
- What do you mean, "we"?

17:52.196 --> 17:53.946
Are you shootin' monsters?

17:53.947 --> 17:55.740
- No.
- Are you shootin' monsters?

17:55.741 --> 17:57.033
- No.
- You are. You are.

17:57.034 --> 17:58.493
- Hey.
- You're shootin' monsters!

17:58.494 --> 17:59.577
Daddy!

17:59.578 --> 18:01.621
There he is! Killer!

18:01.622 --> 18:03.749
Yeah. I missed you, boy.

18:04.208 --> 18:05.209
Hey.

18:07.169 --> 18:09.588
- What y'all up to?
- Well, your wife wants me to build faster.

18:10.214 --> 18:11.756
Did you tell her about the big dial?

18:11.757 --> 18:14.134
Yeah, he told me. Come here, baby.

18:14.676 --> 18:16.553
Ah! You're getting so big.

18:20.599 --> 18:22.850
- You huntin' or...?
- Infected.

18:22.851 --> 18:24.686
What? By yourself?

18:25.604 --> 18:26.605
Yeah.

18:30.067 --> 18:31.484
I gotta go.

18:31.485 --> 18:34.488
You keep gettin' those monsters, Benji.

18:37.825 --> 18:39.033
Oh, you got me.

18:39.034 --> 18:40.536
You got me.

18:41.161 --> 18:42.329
Joel.

18:43.789 --> 18:45.457
You were a refugee too.

19:03.892 --> 19:05.185
It's open.

19:10.149 --> 19:11.567
I'll be right there.

19:33.338 --> 19:35.132
Do you want anything to drink?

19:36.049 --> 19:37.383
What do you have?

19:37.384 --> 19:39.136
Whiskey. Herbal tea.

19:40.470 --> 19:43.098
But the tea's mostly
thistles and dirt, so.

19:56.695 --> 19:57.988
What's the occasion?

19:58.947 --> 20:00.616
It's my birthday.

20:05.204 --> 20:07.331
Well, you wanna start or what?

20:16.965 --> 20:18.966
Shake and stems.
What am I, in high school?

20:18.967 --> 20:21.052
It's winter, Gail.

20:21.053 --> 20:22.346
That never stopped Eugene.

20:23.096 --> 20:24.513
January, February,

20:24.514 --> 20:26.892
the man would grow buds
the size of pinecones.

20:28.393 --> 20:29.519
Sticky as glue.

20:34.107 --> 20:35.234
Payment accepted.

20:43.867 --> 20:46.995
Didn't know psychiatrists were allowed
to drink in these things.

20:47.788 --> 20:49.038
Psychotherapist.

20:49.039 --> 20:50.916
Psychiatrists are the pill ones.

20:51.917 --> 20:54.210
And, no, we're not allowed
to drink in these things.

20:54.211 --> 20:56.671
But I woke up this morning feeling sad.

20:56.672 --> 21:00.968
It's my first birthday
without my husband in 41 years.

21:10.936 --> 21:12.020
Tick, tick, tick.

21:17.734 --> 21:20.611
Well, I tried what you said. I backed off.

21:20.612 --> 21:22.196
I stopped puttin' pressure on her.

21:22.197 --> 21:24.365
Don't even make her sit down with me
for dinner anymore.

21:24.366 --> 21:26.742
And what do I get for it? Nothin'.

21:26.743 --> 21:28.786
She comes home,
shuts herself in the damn garage,

21:28.787 --> 21:31.247
which I should never have
allowed her to move into.

21:31.248 --> 21:33.834
And that's it. Not so much as a hello.

21:35.168 --> 21:36.377
I see her around town.

21:36.378 --> 21:39.171
Gives me a nod like I'm a stranger
or some asshole.

21:39.172 --> 21:41.507
Even Dina asked me today,
"What's wrong with her?"

21:41.508 --> 21:43.010
I mean, everyone can tell.

21:43.802 --> 21:44.886
Now, that one.

21:46.596 --> 21:48.390
That one treats me like a human being.

21:49.474 --> 21:51.767
She talks to me, says "Hello,"

21:51.768 --> 21:53.728
gives me a smile, looks up to me,

21:53.729 --> 21:56.022
makes me feel like I'm a good guy,
which I am.

21:56.023 --> 21:57.565
See, Dina understands me.

21:57.566 --> 21:59.609
Like she's my kid or somethin'.

22:02.321 --> 22:03.405
But she's not.

22:05.532 --> 22:06.533
Neither is Ellie.

22:08.785 --> 22:09.870
Tell you what.

22:11.121 --> 22:12.914
Let's try something different.

22:15.959 --> 22:18.169
- Like what?
- Like not pretending

22:18.170 --> 22:20.714
you have the most boring
problem in the world.

22:21.590 --> 22:23.090
"Oh, a 19-year-old daughter.

22:23.091 --> 22:26.385
"She's acting toward me like
every 19-year-old daughter

22:26.386 --> 22:29.181
has ever acted toward their dad, ever."

22:29.806 --> 22:31.390
What is this, our fifth session?

22:31.391 --> 22:35.144
Are you just gonna keep
grouching on like this every time?

22:35.145 --> 22:37.731
Aren't you supposed to be
validating me or somethin'?

22:38.648 --> 22:41.234
Oh, yeah, actually, I am.

22:42.569 --> 22:45.821
But I'm not gonna do it anymore
because you're lying to me,

22:45.822 --> 22:47.615
and it's exhausting.

22:47.616 --> 22:50.451
Yes, you are, Joel. Yes, you are.

22:50.452 --> 22:54.080
I've done this long enough to know
when somebody is leaving something out.

22:54.081 --> 22:56.958
And you are definitely
leaving something out.

22:57.959 --> 22:59.794
And you want me to validate that?

22:59.795 --> 23:01.295
No.

23:01.296 --> 23:03.173
In fact, fuck, no.

23:08.178 --> 23:10.554
- That's not your first one of the day.
- Oh, no, it isn't.

23:10.555 --> 23:13.182
And before, when I said I was sad,
that wasn't true either.

23:13.183 --> 23:15.101
I'll just come back another day.

23:15.102 --> 23:16.728
Should I say it out loud?

23:19.856 --> 23:21.108
Yeah, I should.

23:24.069 --> 23:26.070
You can't heal something
unless you're brave enough

23:26.071 --> 23:27.656
to say it out loud.

23:32.119 --> 23:33.578
I'm scared though.

23:35.247 --> 23:36.957
I'm scared to say it.

23:37.999 --> 23:39.751
Which is why I have to.

23:43.839 --> 23:46.591
You shot and killed my husband.

23:48.552 --> 23:50.095
You killed Eugene.

23:51.179 --> 23:53.222
And I resent you for it.

23:53.223 --> 23:56.225
No. Maybe a little more than that.

23:56.226 --> 23:58.437
I hate you for it.

23:59.312 --> 24:00.814
I hate you for it.

24:01.773 --> 24:04.108
And, yes, I know you had no choice.

24:04.109 --> 24:06.987
I know that. I know I should forgive you.

24:08.280 --> 24:10.323
Well, I've tried, and I can't

24:11.324 --> 24:14.035
because of how you did it.

24:15.912 --> 24:20.542
And looking at your face
sitting in our home,

24:22.252 --> 24:25.005
makes me so fucking angry.

24:34.014 --> 24:36.850
There it is. I've said it.

24:37.559 --> 24:39.018
I'm ashamed.

24:39.019 --> 24:42.314
But it's in the air
and I can't take it back.

24:46.193 --> 24:49.905
And now, maybe there's a chance
I can make things right with you.

24:53.783 --> 24:54.910
Your turn.

24:56.703 --> 24:59.581
Say the thing you're afraid to say.

25:02.751 --> 25:04.085
I can help you.

25:04.920 --> 25:08.215
Say it out loud, no matter what it is.
No matter how bad.

25:08.840 --> 25:10.800
I promise, I will help.

25:17.098 --> 25:18.808
Did you do something to her?

25:26.191 --> 25:27.858
Did you hurt her?

25:27.859 --> 25:29.860
No. No.

25:29.861 --> 25:31.196
Then, what?

25:32.322 --> 25:34.074
What did you do?

25:56.012 --> 25:57.639
I saved her.

27:05.498 --> 27:07.000
Coming.

27:10.086 --> 27:11.087
Hi.

27:11.838 --> 27:13.005
Came to pick you up.

27:13.006 --> 27:14.090
Oh, you're on this run?

27:16.509 --> 27:17.968
Give me a second.

27:17.969 --> 27:20.930
Take as much time as you need.
Two minutes.

27:22.641 --> 27:25.518
I heard you were getting stuck
on the fence today.

27:26.061 --> 27:27.771
How'd you get out of that?

27:28.688 --> 27:31.024
- Tommy.
- Tommy.

27:33.360 --> 27:34.610
Where'd you get the holster?

27:34.611 --> 27:38.073
Dominique. Traded some old boots for it.

27:41.493 --> 27:42.911
Should've kept the boots.

27:45.205 --> 27:46.246
Here, let me help.

27:46.247 --> 27:47.581
- I can do it.
- It's okay.

27:47.582 --> 27:49.167
I got it. There we go.

27:50.168 --> 27:53.421
Just like that. Hold on.
Let me get this part here.

27:54.506 --> 27:57.884
Yep. 'Cause now-- There we go.

28:00.303 --> 28:02.263
- Better?
- Yeah, better.

28:02.931 --> 28:05.140
Look at you with all that hardware.

28:05.141 --> 28:06.726
You're like Curtis and Viper.

28:08.019 --> 28:09.520
You know those movies Joel likes?

28:09.521 --> 28:11.105
Yeah, I know.

28:11.106 --> 28:12.564
I was actually gonna maybe watch them

28:12.565 --> 28:14.693
tomorrow night with him,
if you wanna join.

28:16.361 --> 28:18.028
Patrol?

28:18.029 --> 28:20.323
Yeah. Yeah, patrol.

28:23.076 --> 28:24.827
- Why, thank you.
- You're welcome.

28:24.828 --> 28:25.954
Yeah.

28:34.963 --> 28:36.463
Hey, Shimmer.

28:36.464 --> 28:38.299
Hi, girl.

28:39.008 --> 28:40.009
Ellie.

28:52.021 --> 28:53.565
There we go.

28:55.316 --> 28:59.486
Okay, we're five minutes behind
because of one or two of you,

28:59.487 --> 29:00.905
so I'll make it short.

29:01.614 --> 29:03.365
You're doing the Alpine run.

29:03.366 --> 29:06.368
I know a couple of you
are new to this trail, so listen up.

29:06.369 --> 29:09.164
You're taking Route 191 down to Hoback.

29:10.915 --> 29:12.040
- Yes, Dina.
- Hi.

29:12.041 --> 29:15.294
Should we stick to the road,
scan the countryside, hit our checkpoints,

29:15.295 --> 29:17.756
and sign the log books?

29:18.798 --> 29:20.966
You know what? That sounds great.

29:20.967 --> 29:23.761
But while you're doing all that,
we've got reports of strays.

29:23.762 --> 29:25.722
So, be careful when you get into the town.

29:26.848 --> 29:29.767
Now, I see Ellie over here
looking like Curtis and Viper.

29:29.768 --> 29:31.894
- The fuck?
- So, let me remind you,

29:31.895 --> 29:34.354
this is just a recon patrol.

29:34.355 --> 29:36.857
If you see one or two runners,
that's fine, clear 'em out.

29:36.858 --> 29:39.193
Anything more, anything worse,

29:39.194 --> 29:41.612
you come on back and we send out a squad.
Understood?

29:41.613 --> 29:44.698
You know you're only, like,
four years older than us, right?

29:44.699 --> 29:46.576
Just say, "Understood."

29:49.621 --> 29:51.663
- Understood.
- Thank you.

29:51.664 --> 29:55.752
Your patrol leader is Kat,
so you will follow her orders.

29:57.295 --> 29:59.713
When you're back,
today's all-clear sign is yellow.

29:59.714 --> 30:02.050
Yellow, good. Green, bad.

30:04.677 --> 30:08.014
Jokes aside, can you take things
a little more seriously?

30:10.892 --> 30:12.310
The others look up to you two.

30:14.103 --> 30:15.814
For some fuckin' reason.

30:17.232 --> 30:20.108
Okay, Alpine run, moving out!

30:20.109 --> 30:22.570
Alpine run! Moving out, let's go!

31:10.869 --> 31:12.828
So, you going tonight?

31:12.829 --> 31:14.414
Yes, I'm going.

31:15.415 --> 31:16.499
Taking anyone?

31:19.294 --> 31:21.254
- No.
- Why not?

31:22.255 --> 31:24.423
- Kat's available.
- Why would I ask Kat?

31:24.424 --> 31:27.510
Because she's the other one.

31:28.177 --> 31:30.262
- Oh, my God.
- What?

31:30.263 --> 31:31.973
You used to with her.

31:32.724 --> 31:34.391
And she definitely left her mark.

31:34.392 --> 31:36.019
Right, yes, thank you.

31:36.853 --> 31:37.896
But no.

31:42.901 --> 31:44.694
You're into someone else.

31:48.489 --> 31:50.449
Tell you what. You can go with me.

31:50.450 --> 31:52.117
We can get baked.

31:52.118 --> 31:54.828
We can dance to the smooth tunes of--
what are they called?

31:54.829 --> 31:57.248
Britney and the Jug Boys. It'll be fun!

31:57.957 --> 31:59.207
We'll count down to the New Year together.

31:59.208 --> 32:01.209
BFFs, 2029.

32:01.210 --> 32:03.337
- Aren't you and Jesse?
- No.

32:03.338 --> 32:04.505
Broke up.

32:05.673 --> 32:06.799
Yes, again.

32:07.634 --> 32:08.635
For now.

32:10.219 --> 32:11.596
What is it with you two?

32:14.140 --> 32:15.433
I don't know.

32:35.620 --> 32:36.621
Let's go.

32:37.705 --> 32:39.791
- Okay. We're on.
- Wait.

32:40.792 --> 32:42.668
We should go back and report it.

32:42.669 --> 32:44.795
We're recon, Kat. Let's fuckin' recon.

32:44.796 --> 32:46.005
Wait, guys!

32:48.049 --> 32:49.717
Hey, come on. Guys!

33:18.663 --> 33:21.666
How many infected does it take
to bring down a bear?

33:23.376 --> 33:24.919
Check out the van.

33:26.379 --> 33:28.130
So, they've been sheltering in the market.

33:28.131 --> 33:30.799
Yeah, it looks like at least one of them
made it back in.

33:30.800 --> 33:33.176
Maybe needed a nap
after chomping that poor thing.

33:33.177 --> 33:34.470
Yeah.

33:36.055 --> 33:37.056
Hey,

33:37.890 --> 33:39.350
what do you call a grizzly's ribs?

33:40.560 --> 33:42.103
Bear-b-cue.

33:46.441 --> 33:47.649
Did you just make that up?

33:47.650 --> 33:49.401
- Yeah.
- Bear-b-cue?

33:49.402 --> 33:50.611
- Yeah.
- Seriously?

33:57.577 --> 33:59.411
So, you think Hungry Boy
is still alive in there?

33:59.412 --> 34:01.038
Fuckin' hope so.

34:01.039 --> 34:02.123
Good.

34:03.916 --> 34:05.250
Hi. Oh, hi there.

34:05.251 --> 34:06.586
- Here comes fun.
- Hi.

34:07.420 --> 34:08.713
Oh, my God.

34:10.631 --> 34:11.632
Happy?

34:17.138 --> 34:18.431
Hey, can we go back now, please?

34:19.057 --> 34:21.224
Yeah, we will. Promise.

34:21.225 --> 34:25.228
We're just gonna listen quick,
see if any are in there,

34:25.229 --> 34:26.897
which is definitely recon.

34:26.898 --> 34:28.398
Hey, you know,
maybe there's a regular person

34:28.399 --> 34:30.275
who's trapped and needs help.

34:30.276 --> 34:32.527
Yeah, what if there's a family in there?

34:32.528 --> 34:35.614
What if there's a toddler? Or a baby?

34:35.615 --> 34:37.575
There's no babies in there.

34:39.327 --> 34:40.911
Hey, come on.

34:40.912 --> 34:42.080
Rules!

34:44.415 --> 34:45.832
Fine.

34:45.833 --> 34:48.085
If you hear anything, you come right back.

34:48.086 --> 34:49.462
Okay.

34:51.631 --> 34:53.132
You just gonna let 'em go in?

34:54.133 --> 34:55.676
I'll give 'em five minutes.

35:02.892 --> 35:04.685
Two on one.

35:17.657 --> 35:19.909
Okay, so one on one.
We've done that before.

35:25.248 --> 35:27.792
If you'd rather let the men handle it.

36:52.793 --> 36:54.045
Two.

36:54.754 --> 36:56.214
The bottle.

38:37.940 --> 38:39.275
Fuck yeah.

38:41.027 --> 38:43.445
Did you get bit?
Do I have to shoot you in the face?

38:43.446 --> 38:45.280
- Not today.
- Okay.

38:45.281 --> 38:46.699
Nice.

38:48.659 --> 38:51.495
Oh, my God, before we leave,
you gotta check out the employee--

38:52.997 --> 38:54.415
Ellie!

38:55.750 --> 38:57.585
Ellie! Ellie!

38:59.170 --> 39:01.088
Ellie, are you okay?

39:04.175 --> 39:05.217
I'm good.

39:08.554 --> 39:12.265
Nothing's broken, I don't think.

39:12.266 --> 39:13.642
Oh, shit.

39:14.477 --> 39:15.644
Are you alone?

39:23.361 --> 39:24.987
I don't hear anything.

39:26.155 --> 39:27.865
I think we're good.

39:38.542 --> 39:42.380
Alright, let's figure out
how to get you out.

39:47.676 --> 39:48.927
I don't see a way out.

39:48.928 --> 39:51.388
- A bunch of padlocked doors.
- Okay.

39:51.389 --> 39:56.059
It's too far for me to drop down,
so I can find a stairway or something

39:56.060 --> 39:57.894
and figure out a path back up here.

39:57.895 --> 39:59.896
- Just stay put.
- Yeah.

39:59.897 --> 40:01.190
Ellie?

40:02.233 --> 40:03.567
Stay put.

40:04.652 --> 40:06.612
- Yeah.
- Alright.

43:04.456 --> 43:06.041
Run at me, fucker!

43:11.130 --> 43:12.298
Run at me!

45:01.198 --> 45:02.408
Fuck.

45:05.452 --> 45:07.830
Ellie, are you okay?! Ellie, it's me!

45:09.164 --> 45:10.374
Over here!

45:13.711 --> 45:15.963
Oh, shit. You okay?

45:16.797 --> 45:17.923
Yeah.

45:21.552 --> 45:23.594
That was it?

45:23.595 --> 45:26.515
- Just her?
- Just her.

45:31.520 --> 45:33.981
So, you're saying it was, what?

45:34.732 --> 45:36.190
Smart?

45:36.191 --> 45:38.109
I'm not saying
it could do math or anything,

45:38.110 --> 45:39.485
but it didn't run at me.

45:39.486 --> 45:43.156
It did what we do--
took cover, planned, waited,

45:43.157 --> 45:45.324
lured me in.

45:45.325 --> 45:46.493
Stalking.

45:48.287 --> 45:49.496
And you saw this?

45:50.622 --> 45:52.332
It was exactly like Ellie says.

45:53.625 --> 45:57.170
And how exactly does you two runnin' into
an uncleared building

45:57.171 --> 46:00.548
qualify as following the rules
and obeying your captain?

46:00.549 --> 46:02.675
Well, it wasn't like
this is our first time.

46:02.676 --> 46:04.719
We've killed a lot of infected before.

46:04.720 --> 46:05.887
And you're telling me, what,

46:05.888 --> 46:07.263
if it were you and Joel,
you wouldn't have gone in?

46:07.264 --> 46:09.557
- Well, that ain't the same.
- Why?

46:09.558 --> 46:11.185
- 'Cause it's different.
- How?

46:14.563 --> 46:19.777
Alright. Apologize to Kat
and log your report with Jesse. Go.

46:30.537 --> 46:31.913
Do we believe them?

46:31.914 --> 46:35.625
Dina was lying. She didn't see anything.
But I believe Ellie.

46:35.626 --> 46:37.836
Maybe this smart one was a one-off.

46:38.545 --> 46:39.796
Maybe.

46:39.797 --> 46:41.881
But what about the other six
that brought down the grizzly?

46:41.882 --> 46:44.759
Yeah, well, six ain't good,
but it's not exactly a horde.

46:44.760 --> 46:46.261
Not yet.

46:47.012 --> 46:49.931
I don't know, just lately,
I've had a feeling.

46:49.932 --> 46:51.433
A feeling?

46:54.102 --> 46:56.605
"Reality is nothing
but a collective hunch."

47:00.025 --> 47:01.860
Lily Tomlin.

47:03.737 --> 47:05.280
Four hours till New Year's.

47:06.323 --> 47:07.616
We adjourned?

47:08.742 --> 47:09.827
Adjourned.

48:39.166 --> 48:40.250
Come in.

48:44.296 --> 48:45.422
Ellie.

48:48.592 --> 48:50.636
- Better?
- Nope.

48:52.554 --> 48:53.680
Okay.

48:56.558 --> 48:59.144
Just come to see if you were going
to that thing tonight.

48:59.978 --> 49:01.396
Be good to show your face.

49:02.147 --> 49:04.398
I don't know. Yeah, maybe.

49:04.399 --> 49:05.776
I don't know.

49:11.865 --> 49:13.450
You been playin' much?

49:15.077 --> 49:16.286
Enough, yeah.

49:30.384 --> 49:31.842
Strings are shot.

49:31.843 --> 49:33.344
- Well--
- I'll put some new ones on for ya.

49:33.345 --> 49:34.679
Oh, you don't have to do that, I--

49:34.680 --> 49:36.306
I can get it back tomorrow.

50:21.476 --> 50:22.769
Oh, sorry!

50:44.958 --> 50:46.709
I hate these things.

50:46.710 --> 50:51.131
Tell me about it.
Had to get half-drunk just to show up.

50:52.841 --> 50:54.509
She's putting on quite the show.

50:55.427 --> 50:56.595
Happy New Year!

51:04.394 --> 51:07.481
You guys will be back
together in two weeks, tops.

51:08.982 --> 51:10.233
Not gonna happen.

51:13.070 --> 51:14.737
- Why?
- Ellie! Hey!

51:14.738 --> 51:16.280
What took you so long?

51:16.281 --> 51:18.699
Okay, this next one is a little slower.

51:18.700 --> 51:21.035
- It's one of our favorites.
- Come on! Let's go!

51:21.036 --> 51:23.621
Hey, don't forget, you got early patrol,
so get some rest.

51:23.622 --> 51:25.332
Sir, yes, sir.

51:39.930 --> 51:42.933
Okay, I have a very serious
question for you.

51:44.267 --> 51:46.353
How bad do I smell?

51:50.398 --> 51:54.318
Like a hot pile of garbage.

51:54.319 --> 51:57.279
Oh, okay.

51:57.280 --> 51:58.782
Yeah.

52:01.326 --> 52:02.536
Gross.

52:03.537 --> 52:04.663
You're so drunk.

52:05.622 --> 52:08.416
I'm high. Smoked a lot.

52:38.905 --> 52:41.283
Every guy in this room
is staring at you right now.

52:46.538 --> 52:49.833
Maybe they're staring at you.

52:52.586 --> 52:54.004
They're not.

52:56.089 --> 52:57.382
Maybe

52:58.049 --> 53:00.427
they're jealous of you.

53:03.597 --> 53:05.015
No reason to be.

53:05.974 --> 53:07.350
I'm not a threat.

53:12.731 --> 53:13.899
Oh, Ellie.

53:16.276 --> 53:19.196
I think they should be terrified of you.

53:44.888 --> 53:45.931
Hey.

53:48.391 --> 53:49.768
It's a family event.

53:51.811 --> 53:53.021
Sorry.

53:57.567 --> 53:58.735
Sorry!

54:02.614 --> 54:04.240
You're in a church.

54:04.241 --> 54:06.033
- Dykes.
- The fuck did you just say?

54:06.034 --> 54:07.619
Ellie, no. Ellie.

54:08.870 --> 54:10.037
Get the hell outta here.

54:10.038 --> 54:11.539
Jesus!

54:12.415 --> 54:14.501
Seth, let's...

54:15.126 --> 54:19.464
Let's take a walk. Come on. Let's go.

54:21.508 --> 54:22.842
Are you okay?

54:23.969 --> 54:25.679
What is wrong with you?

54:30.225 --> 54:32.978
I don't need your fucking help.

54:39.234 --> 54:40.485
Right.

55:10.307 --> 55:11.599
There ya go!

55:14.019 --> 55:15.144
Cheers!

55:15.145 --> 55:18.064
Happy fucking New Year!

56:06.446 --> 56:08.113
- Same thing.
- I know.

56:08.114 --> 56:09.490
We started at the party too, man.

56:09.491 --> 56:10.825
I know.

56:13.620 --> 56:15.996
Oh, my God. Wait up!

56:15.997 --> 56:17.415
Come on, let's go.
